    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">509 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The expulsion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-superbus">Tarquinius Superbus</a> ends Roman kingship and begins the Republic, whose elected magistrates also serve as priests</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">206 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">During the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> the Sibylline books call for the cult of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cybele">Magna Mater</a> from Pessinus</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">186 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The Senate restricts the Bacchanals, a popular mystery cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dionysus">Bacchus</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">64</span><span class="rf-text">After the Great Fire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> blames the Christians, who are persecuted and killed</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">303</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a>’s first edict against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> orders the destruction of churches and Christian texts</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">313</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-milan">Edict of Milan</a> makes mutual toleration the ideology of the empire</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">380</span><span class="rf-text">Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicene-christianity">Nicene Christianity</a> becomes the official state religion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">391</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> ends official support for all other cults and extinguishes the sacred fire of the Vestals</span></li></ol>
    </section>

